 Free text searches titles, conversation content, and bounded single-token directory/path matches. Exact matches are boosted, while fuzzy matching keeps common typos useful.
 
+Emoji such as `💎` are searchable in titles and chat content using the same cached index. Compound emoji match their exact sequence, including skin tones and variation selectors.
+
+To find a session by ID, paste its full ID or type a fragment into the same search box. A single token of 3–64 characters also matches IDs case-insensitively, including characters appearing in order with gaps, as in fzf. Full IDs receive a stronger boost than contiguous fragments, which receive a stronger boost than scattered matches. Very long or complex fragments can fall back to full or contiguous matching. ID searches keep the conversation preview and work with the filters below.
+
+Results show a Session ID column. Narrow layouts abbreviate IDs; the conversation preview header shows the full ID.
+
+Codex rows also show `Original` or `Fork` in the Type column. A fork's preview shows `Fork of:` with the immediate source session ID, which you can paste into search to find that conversation. Forks remain independent sessions and resume under their own IDs. This metadata is cached with the index, so showing it does not read session files while you search.
+
+With the preview open, the session list shows five rows above a larger, full-width chat preview. Arrow keys scroll through every matching session; Page Up and Page Down move five sessions at a time. Ctrl-P hides the preview and expands the list. Very short terminals show fewer rows to keep the preview usable.
+
+Codex previews show the chat: your messages and visible assistant replies. Injected `AGENTS.md` instructions, environment context, internal reasoning, tool payloads, and mirrored log records are excluded from previews and content searches. Installing this version refreshes the cached content once; ordinary searches still use the index.
+
+Codex results show main sessions and regular forks. Subagent threads disappear on the next refresh. Selecting a subagent left in an older cache resumes its main session in the main session's directory, following nested parents when needed. If its parent chain is missing or cyclic, resume is unavailable.
+
+```bash
+fr 019abcde-1234-5678-9abc-def012345678
+fr "agent:codex 9abc"
+```
